<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "1B">
<servcat sctnbr = "01" scnbr = "02">
<configtype typenbr = "2">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1226011" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Pressure Sensor Inspection
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1226010">Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Pressure Sensor Removal and Installation:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
If excessive pressure is applied, the GPF pressure sensor may be damaged.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Do not exceed a pressure of 100 kPa (1.0 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 14.5 psi, 1.0 bar).
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<ptxt>
Measure output voltage of GPF pressure sensor (1) as follows.
</ptxt>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Arrange 3 new 1.5 V batteries (2) in series, and check that total voltage is 4.5 to 5.0 V.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect voltmeter (3) and batteries to GPF pressure sensor as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set special tools as follows.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1B212">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09918-18111">
09918–18111
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1B213">
<s-part>
(B)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09355-35754-601">
09355–35754–601
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Loosen adjusting screw (4) fully.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Connect air hose (5) to special tool.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Connect special tool (A) to GPF pressure sensor using hose (B).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I9P60A122011.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "93.192mm" ver = "02" gw = "207" gh = "248"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
6.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Compressed air
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that output voltage varies as shown in the following graph when pressure applied to sensor is increased up to 100 kPa (1.0 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 14.5 psi, 1.0 bar) from 0 kPa (0 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 0 psi, 0 bar) using special tool and compressed air.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If faulty condition is found, replace GPF pressure sensor. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1226010"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IJAA0A123002.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "51.548mm" ver = "02" gw = "166" gh = "130"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
